ed questions. For this, new algorithm has been proposed.  A QA implementation, usually a computer program, may construct its answers by querying a structured database of knowledge or information, usually a knowledge base. More commonly, QA systems can pull answers from an unstructured collection of natural language documents. Here a similar attempt at solving the problem has been performed, where part of a article from Wikipedia has been used as corpus and was tested against different type of questions that the program can answer correctly. Advanced QA requires sophisticated text processing tools based on state-of-the-art NLP.","topics":[],"score":230450,"global_rank":109173},{"name":"Yueliang-Yu/RPC_java","owner":"Yueliang-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Yueliang-Yu/RPC_java","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":null,"topics":[],"score":230448,"global_rank":109176},{"name":"nesredinahmed/Login","owner":"nesredinahmed","html_url":"https://github.com/nesredinahmed/Login","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":null,"topics":[],"score":230448,"global_rank":109186},{"name":"tamirkifle/skier-tracking-system","owner":"tamirkifle","html_url":"https://github.com/tamirkifle/skier-tracking-system","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":null,"topics":[],"score":230448,"global_rank":109197},{"name":"GaoussouDoucoure/StreamForEach","owner":"GaoussouDoucoure","html_url":"https://github.com/GaoussouDoucoure/StreamForEach","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":null,"topics":[],"score":230448,"global_rank":109219},{"name":"GaoussouDoucoure/LambdaExpressionWithReturn","owner":"GaoussouDoucoure","html_url":"https://github.com/GaoussouDoucoure/LambdaExpressionWithReturn","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":null,"topics":[],"score":230448,"global_rank":109220},{"name":"GaoussouDoucoure/LambdaExpr